From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:55:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(entities): apply authoritative projectile owner changes

Java 26.3 reconstructs an owner from spawn data but has no vanilla packet
for subsequent owner changes. Consume core-resolved ownership only on the
independently advertised projectile channel, preserving both direct and
ViaProxy routes without coupling it to custom actor rendering.

Use per-spawn Java UUIDs and actual local-player identity to reject stale
IDs. Resolve either frontend arrival order, clear unloaded owners, and
restore matching actors through client tracking callbacks. World changes
and disconnects invalidate queued work and release reference state.

Fishing bobbers otherwise discard themselves immediately when Java cannot
resolve their player owner. On Bedrock connections, retain those pending
bobbers for authoritative removal instead. Reassignment clears the prior
player's fishing pointer before invoking Java's normal owner setter.

Core wire and lifecycle tests cover this shared owner registry. Actual
native visible fishing and complete projectile physics remain required
comparisons; this change does not claim full projectile action parity.
